// Two exponential moving averages, the band between them, and a marker on the
// bar where they cross.
//
// Exercises: input of a number and of a source, ema, crossUp and crossDown,
// plot and fill at the top level, signal, and colour names written bare.
//
// The crossing is a signal() call rather than a plotted shape because a
// crossing is an event on one bar, and a column of one value per bar can only
// express it by being absent on every other bar.

version 1

study("EMA cross", overlay = true, precision = 2)

fastLen = input(9,  "Fast length", min = 1, max = 500)
slowLen = input(21, "Slow length", min = 1, max = 500)
src     = input(close, "Source")

fast = ema(src, fastLen)
slow = ema(src, slowLen)

// Both averages are computed unconditionally at the top level. Computing one
// inside the branch that uses it would advance its state only on the bars that
// branch was taken, which is warning OS8001 and a broken line.
up   = crossUp(fast, slow)
down = crossDown(fast, slow)

// Both plots are named. fill shades between two declared columns and takes the
// declaration handles those two names hold, never the series the columns were
// computed from: a band is a field of the chart descriptor holding two plot
// keys, so there is nothing for a bare expression to compile into and an
// expression in either position is OS3020.
fastPlot = plot(fast, "Fast", aqua, width = 2)
slowPlot = plot(slow, "Slow", orange, width = 2)

// The band is drawn between the two plotted columns rather than as a third
// column, so it inherits their warmup: neither average exists before bar 20,
// the values are absent there, and the fill simply starts where they do.
fill(fastPlot, slowPlot, fade(aqua, 90))

if up
    signal("BUY")

if down
    signal("SELL")
